      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e the vmemmap_base being set quite early, couldn\u0027t the host just set the PROTECTED flags directly inside it before deprivilege?\n\nDo you mean having the host pre-populate the hyp_vmemmap, and use that to mark some pages as \u0027protected\u0027?\n\n\u003e That would avoid to have a separated hypercall and to alloc pages for the host s2 too early?\n\nI can see how that could avoid a hypercall (though that would be added complexity in the __pkvm_init path as we would have to walk the entire vmemmap I think?), but not sure how that avoids the early allocation for host s2 pages?",
      "parentUuid": "e266129b_f298b8d7",
      "revId": "d9a0d9b3cbc5de3db7ea7705952b99f7114f734c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
